```js
isComplete(island) {
  if (!this.board || !this.placed) return false;
  let sum = 0;
  for (const edge of this.board.edges) {
    if (edge.a === island.index || edge.b === island.index) {
      sum += this.placed.get(edge.id) ?? 0;
    }
  }
  return sum >= island.num;
}
```

`this.placed` is set in draw() to `bridges` ✓. `island.index` — the islands in board.islands have `index` ✓. The edge's `a`/`b` are the island indices ✓.

Hmm, so sum = 2 for the island with num=2 → 2 >= 2 → true → complete ✓.

So why isn't the strike drawn? Let me check the draw order... 

OH WAIT. The issue might be that the render happened BEFORE the bridge was set? No, setBridge calls render().

