Hmm, my experiment script has a bug: the bridge cells aren't marked in `occ`, so the "free" check doesn't account for bridge cells → the growth could place a bridge over an existing bridge (a crossing). The crossing check handles the perpendicular crossing ✓ but a collinear overlap could occur.

Also I left a nonsense no-op line. Let me clean this up: rather than a separate experimental implementation, let me integrate the feature into the real generator (as an option) and measure it there. That's cleaner and directly usable.

Let me modify `growSolution` in js/generator.js to support:
- `maxLen`: the maximum bridge length (1 = the current behaviour, > 1 = variable lengths)
- `noAdjacent`: reject a new island that is orthogonally adjacent to another island

And a proper "occupied" tracking including bridge cells.

Let me look at the current growSolution implementation and rewrite it properly.

Current implementation (relevant part):
```js
  let guard = 0;
  while (islands.length < target && guard < 6000) {
    guard++;
    const cands = [];
    const weights = [];

    for (let i = 0; i < islands.length; i++) {
      const isl = islands[i];
      for (const d of DIRS) {
        for (const dist of [1, 2]) {
          const nr = isl.r + d.dr * dist;
          const nc = isl.c + d.dc * dist;
          if (nr < 0 || nr >= rows || nc < 0 || nc >= cols) continue;
          if (islandAt(islands, nr, nc)) continue;
          if (dist === 2) {
            const mr = isl.r + d.dr;
            const mc = isl.c + d.dc;
            if (islandAt(islands, mr, mc)) continue;
          }
          if (liesOnBridge(islands, edges, nr, nc)) continue;
          if (crossesExisting(islands, edges, isl.r, isl.c, nr, nc)) continue;
          ...
        }
      }
    }
    ...
    islands.push({ r: chosen.r, c: chosen.c });
    edges.push({ a: chosen.parent, b: id, w: ... });
  }
```

The checks are:
- The new island's cell is free ✓
- The intermediate cell (for dist 2) has no island ✓
- The new island doesn't lie on an existing bridge ✓
- The new segment doesn't cross an existing bridge ✓

For variable lengths, I need:
- All the intermediate cells (1..len-1) must be free of islands AND bridges
- The new island's cell must be free
- The new segment must not cross an existing bridge
- The new island must not lie ON an existing bridge (liesOnBridge) — hmm, if the intermediate cells are free of bridges, then the new island can't lie on a bridge either... but a bridge could pass through the new island's cell (perpendicular) → that's a crossing → caught by crossesExisting ✓.

Let me restructure the loop to iterate over the directions and the lengths 1..maxLen:
```js
